  Further budget/continuity matrix reduction (approved by the user on 2026-11-03)
    The remaining 30 budget and 24 continuity cases had not received the same representative-axis
    reduction as the diagnostics. The user approved 17 budget and seven continuity cases,
    retaining the 14 diagnostics unchanged: 38 primary cases total, 30 fewer than the prior 68.
    This is failure-mode sampling with explicitly reduced combination coverage, not a claim that
    every removed input can never reveal a regression. Production code remains unchanged.
    Approved diagnostic sampling principles also apply to these shared-kernel fixtures: budgets
    select loop ceilings, while full/half decoding has dedicated independent witnesses. Current
    production compiled quality/resolution tests remain separate from these dynamic selectors.
    Approved budget selection (17 rows across all six existing methods):
      ClippedEndpointPreservesFallback: retain quality 3, both resolutions, normal and tiny
      extents (4 rows; remove 4 lower-budget normal rows). The largest ceiling proves the
      two-probe early stop rather than merely exhausting a low ceiling. Normal extents cross
      texture footprints; tiny positive extents stay within one footprint. Both resolutions
      retain endpoint/fallback equivalence and the independent accepted-endpoint control.
      RayAndUvTransitionsStayWithinReceiverFootprint: retain slope 4 at full and half size
      (2 rows; remove the two slope-1 rows). Keep all 61 positions and every independent
      Snell/plane/RGB/transition assertion. Full-size geometric-hit and half-size actual-switch
      witnesses remain; the second, milder slope/input-motion range is no longer sampled here.
      CachedPatchRequiresRepresentedCoverage: retain both rows (2). Regular support supplies
      the independent corrected-hit color witness. Irregular support detects immediate reuse
      outside its represented hull, although its current two-evaluation assertion remains an
      incomplete final-validity oracle. This reduction does not silently strengthen or delete it.
      ExhaustionAndTirAccountForEveryLookup: retain all four current rows. These independently
      check all three mapped ceilings/endpoint termination and the distinct zero-evaluation TIR
      early exit; other reduced tests need not repeat every budget to prove those contracts.
      ExhaustedFallbackReusesInitialSupport: retain quality 3 at full and half size (2 rows;
      remove 4 lower-quality rows). Preserve all five internal scenes and three compared modes.
      The high-budget invalid-seed scene reaches later valid support before exhaustion, making
      it an adversarial check that later recovery cannot replace the original invalid seed.
      Both resolutions retain edge-footprint saved-read differences and fallback equivalence.
      TierSelectionTracksDenseReference: retain quality 1 full/half and quality 3 half (3 rows;
      remove the other 3). Keep all four internal fields and all seven positions per field.
      The full low-budget case retains the absolute CPU intersection/motion oracle; low-budget
      half retains approximate-UV footprint checks. High-budget half currently reaches geometric
      floor results at positions where the low-budget case falls back, and reaches farther through
      gaps. These outcomes are observed regimes, not newly asserted ray-count guarantees.
      Mid-budget behavior and high-budget full-size combinations lose this dense-reference
      witness; independent ceiling, fallback, raw discontinuity and compiled-variant checks remain.
